dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960887654050095134":{"a":"<p>@rrichcord OK, I have been thinking on this all day. I think we have a bunch of things coming into phase. That is the midpoint between Superior Conjuction of Saturn/Neptune start of period and peak of period. 25% Through the cycle. 177 days since 3/3/2025 and 177 days until Feb 20, 2026.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1960746329703149735\">https://x.com/i/status/1960746329703149735</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1960887654050095134</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1960887654050095134\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2025-08-28T02:10:22Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960889957490323844":{"a":"<p>@rrichcord New moon transition to waxing crescent I think acts kinda like a lens with its event horizon. When the Sun hits a certain point we get a high impedance reflection point in time along that path in space. Manifests gaps in our perception of energy which can be found time-shifted…</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1960887654050095134\">https://x.com/i/status/1960887654050095134</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1960889957490323844</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1960889957490323844\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2025-08-28T02:19:32Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960890284197507571":{"a":"<p>@rrichcord A sort of repeating pattern that appears to us to be diced up over time. Kinda like a prism for time.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1960889957490323844\">https://x.com/i/status/1960889957490323844</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1960890284197507571</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1960890284197507571\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2025-08-28T02:20:49Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960890701702685069":{"a":"<p>@rrichcord If we think of the 177 days above as 4 quaters of a sine wave. Then we would be at min impedance.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1960890284197507571\">https://x.com/i/status/1960890284197507571</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1960890701702685069</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1960890701702685069\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2025-08-28T02:22:29Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960894351988400488":{"a":"<p>Pepsidynamics we might call it. It&#x27;s like Electrodynamics but with fizzy soda. <a href=\"https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1960788890861887588\">Tweet by @BrianRoemmele</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1960788890861887588\">https://x.com/BrianRoemmele/status/1960788890861887588</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1960894351988400488</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1960894351988400488\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2025-08-28T02:36:59Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1960895398202978575":{"a":"<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xPSDxfSdRb8\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/xPSDxfSdRb8\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"acc